    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against right-handed pitching. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is the primary engine today, pairing a high-floor base projection with a 14% boost for his dynamic platoon advantage against Lopez. **Jacob Wilson** remains an essential start despite the pending lineup confirmation; assuming he hits second against Framber Valdez, he leverages a 10% park boost and a strong offensive environment to maintain elite efficiency. **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.88) round out our top-tier plays, both capitalizing on soft matchups against Mikolas and Avila, respectively, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.51) remains a locked-in asset due to his high-volume production in the two-hole, even against a relatively tough arm in Mathews.\n\nNavigating the peripheral categories\u2014specifically our mandate to prioritize stolen bases\u2014the optimizer faced a difficult choice regarding the UTIL slot. **Nasim Nunez** (57.91) edged out **Denzer Guzman** (45.62) for that spot, primarily due to **Nasim Nunez**'s utility versatility and superior efficiency in the optimizer's current model. **Denzer Guzman** and **Wade Meckler** were both sidelined due to lingering lineup uncertainty against Gasser, while **Sam Antonacci** provided the stiffest competition, falling just short of the start threshold due to a difficult matchup against the sharp Rasmussen, which dampened his overall projection despite his favorable batting order slot. \n\nWe must monitor the situation surrounding **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**, whose scores (53.01 and 56.20) are being dragged down by an elite opposing pitcher in Sanchez and a defensive setup that suppresses stolen base opportunities. While their park factors and tailwinds are positive, the high degree of risk against a sub-3.00 xERA arm means they are starts based on raw talent rather than an ideal matchup. Finally, keep an eye on the official lineups for **Jacob Wilson** and **Heliot Ramos**; should they slide down the order from the assumed #2 spot, their efficiency scores will likely recalibrate, though they currently remain protected as strong recommendations for our 5x5 rotation.",
